@format 1
@id media-preview.common.media-publication
@title Media publication
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry cargo-ready
@summary Trace PViewerMediaRaise accurately: one multicast invocation is protected by one try/catch, so a throwing subscriber prevents later subscribers in that invocation from running.
@related media-preview.common.flyleaf-preview, media-preview.common.mpv-preview, media-preview.in-edit, media-removal.in-global-interface
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag publication

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias source = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSource
@alias info = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PInfo
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace

[cargo-ready] Viewer cargo ready for event publication <input>
~ The preview has new media information ready to announce.
[Technical explanation]
= A backend failure, viewer close, restricted source, or preview commit has called PViewerMediaRaise with an LCargo.
> publish

[publish] Multicast PViewerMediaChange invocation <decision>
~ The preview panel tells its listeners that the current media has changed.
[Technical explanation]
- Invoke the PViewerMediaChange multicast delegate once inside one try/catch; unlike LMediaLoadRaise, handlers are not enumerated and isolated individually @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
? "No attached subscriber throws" > subscriber-effects
? "A subscriber throws" > subscriber-short-circuit

[subscriber-effects] Applicable subscribers complete <process>
~ This step handles applicable subscribers complete.
[Technical explanation]
- When attached, the active-window handler attaches or clears flow media state @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
- When attached, Source synchronizes its displayed source path @ source.PSourceMediaHandle(...)
- When attached, Info synchronizes processability, preview availability, parsed media information, or failure state @ info.PInfoMediaHandle(...)
- Each applicable non-Audio workspace whose viewer and flow both exist attaches PWorkspaceMediaHandle; it remembers applicable sources and schedules or clears LosslessCut discovery @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaHandle(...)
- A temporary relay-load handler, when installed, removes itself on this first media event and restores relay sections only when media information and flow are available @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
! Audio intentionally does not attach PWorkspaceMediaHandle. Edit adds its own PViewerMediaChange subscriber; that scenario-specific restoration is shown in In Edit tab. Which handlers are attached and their invocation order depend on the particular viewer/workspace construction and current window attachment.
> publication-result

[subscriber-short-circuit] Later media subscribers skipped <output>
~ This path ends with later media subscribers skipped.
[Technical explanation]
= PViewerMediaRaise swallows the thrown exception, but normal multicast invocation has already stopped at that subscriber, so handlers later in the invocation list do not run for this cargo.

[publication-result] Attached media subscribers completed <output>
~ This path ends with attached media subscribers completed.
[Technical explanation]
= Every subscriber that was attached and reached without an earlier exception has processed the cargo; control then returns to the caller of PViewerMediaRaise.
